# Claude Code's Bash sandbox mounts /dev/null over the protected paths a repo root lacks, so
# they appear, inside the sandbox only, as character devices, and `git add -A` fails ("can only
# add regular files"). Directory names are ignored only when they aren't directories (`/x`,
# then `!/x/`), so a real new .vscode/ or .claude/skills/ still shows up. A real new FILE with
# one of these names (say a first .claude/settings.json) needs `git add -f`.
/.bash_profile
/.bashrc
/.profile
/.zprofile
/.zshrc
/.gitconfig
/.gitmodules
/.ripgreprc
/.claude/launch.json
/.claude/loop.md
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
/.claude/settings.json
/.idea
!/.idea/
/.vscode
!/.vscode/
/.claude/agents
!/.claude/agents/
/.claude/commands
!/.claude/commands/
/.claude/output-styles
!/.claude/output-styles/
/.claude/routines
!/.claude/routines/
/.claude/skills
!/.claude/skills/
/.claude/workflows
!/.claude/workflows/
